<Legal title="Scout Help and Customer Support" fullTitle="How to Start Your First Job Application | Scout Support" description="Start your first application with Scout: open your dashboard, check your job profile, activate a plan, start applying, then track every submission.">
  <p>Need a hand? We're here to help you get the most out of Scout.</p>

  <h2>How do I start my first application?</h2>
  <p>Here is the short version for the AI Assistant:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open your dashboard: <a href="https://applyscout.app">https://applyscout.app</a>
      <ul>
        <li>Your resume and job profile are saved there when you sign up. You choose Human or AI and import your resume at signup, and Scout shows you the data it extracted from your resume to review.</li>
        <li>You do not need to book a call to get to your dashboard. (Using a Human Assistant? <a href="/book-call">Book a free 15-minute call</a> to ask anything first.)</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      Check that your target roles, locations and dealbreakers say what you actually want. Bad targeting means bad applications.
      <ul>
        <li>Your job profile holds your target roles, locations, salary floor and dealbreakers. Scout matches jobs against it.</li>
        <li>You can create more than one job profile if you are searching for different kinds of roles.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      Activate a plan from your dashboard
      <ul>
        <li>Your dashboard opens with your profile saved. Activate a plan there to begin.</li>
        <li>AI Assistant plans start at $39 a month. See <a href="/pricing">plans and pricing</a>. Prepay 90 days and save about 10%.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      Start your first applications and watch them land in your tracker, with the resume used for each one.
      <ul>
        <li>Scout finds matching jobs for your profile. If you spot a role yourself, add it from your dashboard or with the <a href="/download">Scout for Chrome extension</a>, and choose which job profile and resume it should use.</li>
        <li>You decide whether Scout tailors a copy of your resume to each job or uses your original.</li>
        <li>You can allow automatic approval for routine matches, or require approval for every role. See <a href="/safety">how Scout keeps applications safe</a>.</li>
        <li>Your tracker shows each job, its status, the submission time and the resume used.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>Stuck on any step? Email <a href="mailto:support@applyscout.app">support@applyscout.app</a> and we usually reply within one business day.</p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@applyscout.app">support@applyscout.app</a> and we'll get back to you, usually within one business day.</p>

